  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Data, information and types of data"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Data is raw facts and figures, such as numbers, text, images or sounds. When data is processed and given context, it becomes information that helps in making decisions. Structured data is organised in rows and columns, like a table of student records. Unstructured data has no fixed format, such as photos, videos, audio and social media posts. Semi-structured data has some organisation through tags or keys but not a strict table, such as an email with header fields or an HTML or XML document."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Data → processing → information"
    },
    {
     "en": "Structured: tables, spreadsheets"
    },
    {
     "en": "Semi-structured: email, HTML/XML, JSON"
    },
    {
     "en": "Unstructured: images, audio, video, free text"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "Data is raw facts and figures, such as numbers, text, images or sounds. When data is processed and given context, it becomes information that helps in making decisions. Structured data is organised in rows and columns, like a table of student records. Unstructured data has no fixed format, such as photos, videos, audio and social media posts. Semi-structured data has some organisation through tags or keys but not a strict table, such as an email with header fields or an HTML or XML document.",
    "kn": "ದತ್ತಾಂಶ ಎಂದರೆ ಕಚ್ಚಾ ಸಂಗತಿಗಳು. ಅದನ್ನು ಸಂಸ್ಕರಿಸಿ ಸಂದರ್ಭ ನೀಡಿದಾಗ ಮಾಹಿತಿ ಆಗುತ್ತದೆ. ಸಾಲು-ಕಾಲಂಗಳಲ್ಲಿರುವ ದತ್ತಾಂಶ ರಚಿತ (structured), ಫೋಟೋ-ವಿಡಿಯೋಗಳಂತಹವು ಅರಚಿತ (unstructured), ಟ್ಯಾಗ್‌ಗಳಿರುವ ಇಮೇಲ್, XML ಮುಂತಾದವು ಅರೆ-ರಚಿತ ದತ್ತಾಂಶ."
   }
