   "title": {
    "en": "Handling data"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Data capturing is gathering data from sources, for example a biometric attendance machine or an online form. Data storage keeps it on devices such as hard disks, SSDs and the cloud. Data retrieval fetches it when needed. When a file is deleted, usually only its address entry is removed and the space is marked free, so the data can often be recovered with special tools until it is overwritten. This is why devices should be wiped securely before they are sold."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Capture → store → retrieve"
    },
    {
     "en": "Deleted data can often be recovered until it is overwritten"
    },
    {
     "en": "Wipe storage securely before disposing of a device"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "Data capturing is gathering data from sources, for example a biometric attendance machine or an online form. Data storage keeps it on devices such as hard disks, SSDs and the cloud. Data retrieval fetches it when needed. When a file is deleted, usually only its address entry is removed and the space is marked free, so the data can often be recovered with special tools until it is overwritten. This is why devices should be wiped securely before they are sold.",
    "kn": "ದತ್ತಾಂಶ ಸಂಗ್ರಹಣೆ (capturing), ಶೇಖರಣೆ (storage), ಮರುಪಡೆಯುವಿಕೆ (retrieval) ದತ್ತಾಂಶ ನಿರ್ವಹಣೆಯ ಹಂತಗಳು. ಫೈಲ್ ಅಳಿಸಿದಾಗ ಸಾಮಾನ್ಯವಾಗಿ ಅದರ ವಿಳಾಸ ಮಾತ್ರ ತೆಗೆಯಲಾಗುತ್ತದೆ; ಹೀಗಾಗಿ ಹೊಸ ದತ್ತಾಂಶ ಬರೆಯುವವರೆಗೆ ಅದನ್ನು ಮರುಪಡೆಯಬಹುದು."
   }
